    "faq": {
      "heading": "Frequently asked questions",
      "items": [
        { "q": "Is PropHammer free?", "a": "Yes — search, map view and filters are completely free, even without an account. An account is only needed for extras like the watchlist and saved searches." },
        { "q": "Which countries does the data come from?", "a": "PropHammer crawls court and official portals across many European countries as well as curated sources in North America. You can see the exact country list in the search filters." },
        { "q": "How up to date is the data?", "a": "A background crawler keeps the data continuously updated — you never have to trigger anything manually." },
        { "q": "Does PropHammer replace legal advice?", "a": "No. PropHammer provides research data, not legal advice. The listing page lets you contact a referred lawyer directly if you need one." },
        { "q": "What does the AI summary do?", "a": "It summarizes property data, location and condition from appraisals and listings, and translates them on demand — at the push of a button, right on the listing page." },
        { "q": "Does the acquisition-cost calculator work for all countries?", "a": "No, currently only for German foreclosure auctions." }
      ]
